1. Model weights and builds
---------------------------

The base model "general" (camera and microphone):

  decidio/base/general/out/model.keras
  decidio/base/general/out/model_int8.tflite
  decidio/base/general/out/model.dcd

  Every build for a board with a microphone carries this model:
  installer/builds/xiao_sense/*.dcd (made by tools/make_builds.py), and every
  package that `decidio install` sends to such a board.

  Trained on:
  - COCO 2017 train2017 photos and annotations (cocodataset.org).
    Annotations: CC BY 4.0. Photos: the Flickr licence of each photo.
  - ESC-50, folds 2 to 5 (K. J. Piczak). CC BY-NC 3.0: non-commercial use only.
  - Speech Commands v0.02 (Google). CC BY 4.0.
  - LibriSpeech dev-clean (openslr.org). CC BY 4.0.
  - WeatherNet-05-18039 (Hugging Face, prithivMLmods). Its uploader lists it
    as Apache 2.0. The origin of the photos is not stated.
  - Starting point of the vision body: ImageNet-pretrained MobileNetV1 weights
    from Keras. Apache 2.0.

  Because of ESC-50, do not use this model or the builds that carry it for
  commercial purposes.

The base model "general-cam" (camera only):

  decidio/base/general-cam/out/model.keras
  decidio/base/general-cam/out/model_int8.tflite
  decidio/base/general-cam/out/model.dcd

  Every build for a board without a microphone carries this model:
  installer/builds/s3cam/*.dcd, and every package that `decidio install` sends
  to such a board.

  Trained on the COCO 2017 photos, the WeatherNet-05-18039 photos and the
  MobileNetV1 weights listed above. It contains no sound data.


2. Data tables in this repository
---------------------------------

  decidio/starter_data/coco_starter.json.gz
    A list of COCO 2017 val2017 photos with their annotations.
    Annotations: CC BY 4.0. The photos are not included.

  decidio/starter_data/esc50_starter.csv
    The file names and labels of ESC-50 fold 1 (K. J. Piczak).
    CC BY-NC 3.0. The sound files are not included.

  firmware/main/fly/circuit_data.h
  firmware/main/fly/optic_lobe_data.h
    Connection tables derived from the male-cns v1.0 connectome of
    Drosophila melanogaster (Janelia FlyEM Project and the University of
    Cambridge). CC BY 4.0. These tables are also compiled into the firmware.


3. Third-party code in the firmware binaries
--------------------------------------------

The prebuilt firmware (decidio/firmware_bins/esp32s3/*.bin and
installer/builds/firmware.bin) is compiled from firmware/ together with these
components. Their source is not in this repository.

  ESP-IDF 5.5 (Espressif Systems)          Apache-2.0. It includes third-party
                                           components under their own licences,
                                           for example FreeRTOS (MIT), lwIP
                                           (BSD-3-Clause), Mbed TLS (Apache-2.0)
                                           and cJSON (MIT).
  espressif/esp-tflite-micro (TensorFlow Lite Micro)   Apache-2.0
  espressif/esp-nn                                     Apache-2.0
  espressif/esp32-camera                               Apache-2.0
  espressif/mdns                                       Apache-2.0

The browser installer (installer/index.html) loads ESP Web Tools from
unpkg.com when the page opens (Apache-2.0). It is not in this repository.
